From a68101bc49db646de6c60d874ff0f7cca8822499 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: vkd3d-crossover <noreply@vkd3d-crossover.invalid>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 01:12:10 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 26/28] feat: hoist indirect-count conversions in front of
 render passes

Problem: PRAGMATA SKETCHBOOK GPU-bound: the G-buffer was split into 73 render passes (187 per frame).

Root cause: Metal has no indirect-count draws; MoltenVK converted each one with a compute dispatch at the draw, ending and restarting the Metal render pass (store + reload of every attachment).

Fix: When a render pass begins, look ahead to its end and encode the conversions of all its indirect-count draws first; the draws use the pre-converted arguments. Inside a render pass the indirect and count buffers can only change through shader writes.

Verified by: Median fps 12.4 -> 15.5 (+25%), render passes per frame 187 -> 66; all 8 execute_indirect tests identical with and without the hoist.

Off switch: MVK_HOIST_INDIRECT_COUNT=0
---
